/**
 * Swallow the deny inside `catch` so the conformance runner observes a
 * clean exit and the `expect_deny_events` sidecar assertion is the only
 * signal. The sibling `null_*_denies.harn` fixtures use ambient
 * `println("caught")` for the same trick; we omit it here because
 * `harn fix`'s ambient-stdio repair would rewrite that call into a
 * second `harness.stdio.println` whose own null-mode deny event would
 * poison the assertion.
 */
fn main(harness: Harness) {
  try {
    harness.random.gen_u64()
  } catch (e) {
  }
}
